# US-equities exchange calendar: the NYSE and Nasdaq trading schedule (trading domain spec §2.2,
# §4.3), read by `mandate_time::ExchangeCalendar`.
#
# Times are America/New_York wall-clock times; `mandate-time` converts them to UTC with the bundled
# time-zone database, so daylight-saving changes never live in this file.
#
# Records, one per line; `#` starts a comment line, and blank lines are ignored:
#   valid <first date> <last date>
#       The dates this file answers for. A question about any other date is an error.
#   hours <pre-market open> <regular open> <regular close> <after-hours close>
#       The sessions of a full trading day. The overnight session of a trading day runs from the
#       after-hours close on the previous calendar day to the pre-market open.
#   closed <date> <label>
#       A weekday with no session at all. Weekends are always closed and are not listed.
#   early_close <date> <regular close> <after-hours close> <label>
#       A trading day whose regular and after-hours sessions end early.
# Dates are listed in increasing order, each at most once.
#
# Provenance (retrieved 2026-09-26):
# - Alpaca Trading API `GET /v2/calendar?start=2015-01-01&end=2029-12-31` on the paper host
#   (paper-api.alpaca.markets), the broker the spec names as the calendar's source. Every record
#   below was generated from it: the weekdays it omits are `closed`, and the days whose `close` is
#   13:00 and `session_close` 1700 are `early_close`. Every other day it lists opens at 09:30 and
#   04:00 and closes at 16:00 and 20:00, as `hours` states.
# - NYSE, "Holidays & Trading Hours" (https://www.nyse.com/markets/hours-calendars): the live page
#   for 2026 to 2028, and the Internet Archive's copies of it that list 2017 to 2019
#   (web.archive.org/web/2017), 2018 to 2021 (2018), 2021 to 2023 (2020), 2022 to 2024 (20220301),
#   2023 to 2025 (2022), and 2024 to 2026 (2023), including each year's early closes at 1:00 p.m.
#   with late trading sessions closing at 5:00 p.m. Every holiday and early close of 2018 to 2028
#   agrees with the records below; `crates/mandate-time/tests/session.rs` checks them against
#   those lists typed independently.
# - NYSE Group press releases for the two unscheduled closures: "New York Stock Exchange to Honor
#   President George H. W. Bush" (2018-12-05) and "The New York Stock Exchange Will Close Markets
#   on January 9 to Honor the Passing of Former President Jimmy Carter" (2025-01-09).
# - Nasdaq Trader, "U.S. Equity and Options Markets Holiday Schedule 2026"
#   (https://www.nasdaqtrader.com/trader.aspx?id=calendar): the same 2026 closures and early closes
#   as NYSE.
# - The same NYSE page for the session bounds: NYSE Arca Equities' early trading session opens at
#   4:00 a.m., the core session runs 9:30 a.m. to 4:00 p.m., and the late trading session closes at
#   8:00 p.m. (spec §4.3 uses the same hours).
#
# Alpaca's calendar stops listing days after 2029-12-24 and NYSE publishes three years ahead, so
# this file ends at 2028-12-31. Extend it only from a newly published schedule.

valid 2018-01-01 2028-12-31
hours 04:00 09:30 16:00 20:00
closed 2018-01-01 New Year's Day
closed 2018-01-15 Martin Luther King, Jr. Day
closed 2018-02-19 Washington's Birthday
closed 2018-03-30 Good Friday
closed 2018-05-28 Memorial Day
early_close 2018-07-03 13:00 17:00 Day before Independence Day
closed 2018-07-04 Independence Day
closed 2018-09-03 Labor Day
closed 2018-11-22 Thanksgiving Day
early_close 2018-11-23 13:00 17:00 Day after Thanksgiving
closed 2018-12-05 National Day of Mourning for President George H. W. Bush
early_close 2018-12-24 13:00 17:00 Christmas Eve
closed 2018-12-25 Christmas Day
